From: GapKeep <noreply@gapkeep.org>
Subject: dwhci: bound the time the system waits on control transfers

The main loop waits for control transfers: enumeration (plug and play)
and keyboard LEDs. Since 0003 one gives up after 3 s, but a device could
still freeze the system 3 s at a time: by timing out on request after
request, by disconnecting and reconnecting to be enumerated again, or, as
a keyboard that NAKs SET_REPORT, on every Caps Lock.

- After USB_CONTROL_MAX_TIMEOUTS (2) timed-out control transfers, a
  device's control transfers fail at once, until it is replugged (a new
  CUSBDevice).
- Full-length timeouts are budgeted across devices: 3 of them, then one
  more per minute. Past that, control transfers give up after 250 ms, so
  a device that keeps reconnecting cannot freeze the system for long.
- ControlMessage() takes an optional, shorter timeout. The keyboard's
  LED requests get 100 ms, and after one failure no more are sent.

diff --git a/include/circle/usb/dwhcidevice.h b/include/circle/usb/dwhcidevice.h
index e3c0051..1d2978c 100644
--- a/include/circle/usb/dwhcidevice.h
+++ b/include/circle/usb/dwhcidevice.h
@@ -43,6 +43,18 @@
 // device 5 s for a request with no data stage, 500 ms per data packet)
 #define USB_CONTROL_TIMEOUT_MS	3000
 
+// gapkeep: the main loop waits for control transfers (enumeration, keyboard
+// LEDs), so timeouts are bounded: a device's control transfers fail at once
+// after USB_CONTROL_MAX_TIMEOUTS of them timed out, until it is replugged;
+// and, since a device can disconnect and reconnect by itself, timeouts are
+// budgeted across devices: USB_CONTROL_TIMEOUT_CREDIT of them may take the
+// full time, then one more per USB_CONTROL_CREDIT_MS; beyond that a control
+// transfer gives up after USB_CONTROL_SHORT_TIMEOUT_MS.
+#define USB_CONTROL_MAX_TIMEOUTS	2
+#define USB_CONTROL_TIMEOUT_CREDIT	3
+#define USB_CONTROL_CREDIT_MS		60000
+#define USB_CONTROL_SHORT_TIMEOUT_MS	250
+
 class CDWHCIDevice : public CUSBHostController
 {
 public:
